# Environment. `.env.example` and `.env.development` are committed on purpose —
# one is a template, the other only carries the demo flag. Anything that could
# hold a real Supabase key stays out, because a leaked key is not fixed by a
# revert.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.development
